wayvnc types what the person types, whatever their keyboard layout: keysyms,
not key positions, and keysyms outside its keymap on spare keys it sends a
new keymap for, as Xvnc does. Keycodes above 255, which Chromium drops, are
never used. Set WAYVNC_KEYCODES to take QEMU extended key events again.

